id: pm-vcs-jj9r
title: Clone builds a working tree from a remote and inherits its record configuration
description: "A clone that starts from the default configuration is worse than no clone: the source repository declares which paths hold structured records and how their fields merge, and a clone missing those declarations stores the same files as blobs and merges them line by line. The two repositories then disagree about what their shared history means. The transport therefore advertises the source configuration and clone adopts it before it writes a single object."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: "area:vcs",distribution
